WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.390
Dr. Blast and his group of researchers stand
behind bulletproof viewing glass.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:09.000
They all have very serious looks on their
faces, that is until the first test begins.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.639
On one side of the test room a Class-D subject
stands holding a sheet of paper; on the other

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:16.610
side sits a bright red tomato on a wooden
table.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.380
Dr. Blast pushes the intercom button and speaks
into the microphone: “alright, you may begin.”

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.890
D-504-1 nods and looks down at the sheet of
paper in his hand.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.890
He begins to read.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.250
"Is a hippopotamus a hippopotamus or just
a really cool opotamous?"

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.730
Nothing happens.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.460
D-504-1 stands there awkwardly waiting.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.430
A man next to Dr. Blast in the observation
room snickers.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.550
Dr. Blast jerks his head towards the researcher
and stares him down.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.270
“This is not a laughing matter,” Blast
says.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.620
The reprimanded researcher clears his throat
and stands up straight.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.900
“Sorry sir.”

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.760
Dr. Blast leans over and pushes the microphone
button again.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.190
“Proceed to the next joke D-504-1.”

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.980
The man on the other side of the glass nods
and pulls a second sheet of paper out from

00:00:58.980 --> 00:00:59.980
behind the first.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.640
"What's an archaeologist?

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.629
Someone whose career is in ruins," says D-504-1.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:09.830
A moment after he finishes the joke, the ripe
red tomato launches itself off of the table

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.300
and flies towards the face of D-504-1.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.450
The tomato is clocked at moving 104 miles
per hour.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:20.980
D-504-1 has no time to move before the tomato
slams into his nose, instantly breaking it.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.550
The men in the observation room behind the
bulletproof glass do their best to hold back

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.610
their laughter.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.790
Dr. Blast grumbles as he jots down notes on
his clipboard.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.530
“It appears that SCP-504 has a certain "taste"
in jokes,” he says to the rest of the researchers

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.170
in the room, this elicits a slight chuckle.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.580
“This might indicate sapience.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.580
I hope not.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.740
Clean the room and bring in the next subject.”

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.830
Medical personnel and a team of custodial
staff enter the room.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:49.620
The physicians tend to D-504-1’s nose and
carry him out, the custodians clean the remnants

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.480
of tomato off the floor, walls, and ceiling.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.060
They exit, leaving the room completely empty.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.940
A moment later the door opens and another
ordinary looking tomato is brought in and

00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.990
placed on the desk.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.299
The SCP agent who brought in the tomato leaves.

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:07.440
D-504-2 enters the room a moment later with
a sheet of paper in his hand.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.940
He stands on the far side of the room away
from the SCP-504 tomato sitting on the table.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.090
He nervously brings the paper closer to his
face to read what’s on it.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:21.150
“Three tomatoes are walking down the street,”
D-504-2 says with a little shake in his voice.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:26.630
He had seen D-504-1 exit the room just before
he entered, with blood and tomato paste running

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:27.630
down his face.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.350
“A papa tomato, a mama tomato, and a little
baby tomato.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.360
Baby tomato starts lagging behind.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.150
Papa tomato gets angry, goes over to the baby
tomato, and smushes him… and says, catch

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.150
up."

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:45.030
The new SCP-504 tomato immediately goes flying
from the table straight towards the joke teller.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:51.520
This time the tomato is clocked at 264 miler
per hour when it slams into the face of D-504-2

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.130
The impact immediately renders him unconscious.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.959
After the first few trials Dr. Blast decides
that it is time to take things up a notch.

00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:03.270
The Foundation has collected hundreds of SCP-504
tomatoes, so there is no shortage.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.849
After the room is cleaned once again, and
a medical team removes the unconscious Class-D

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:11.602
personnel who was knocked out by the previous
SCP-504 experiment, they are ready to begin

00:03:11.602 --> 00:03:12.602
again.

00:03:12.602 --> 00:03:15.570
This time there will be terrible consequences
for their actions.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.990
D-504-3 enters the room.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:21.010
The SCP-504 tomato has already been placed
on the table.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.270
“You may begin,” Dr. Blast says into the
microphone.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.390
The Class-D personnel reads the joke on the
sheet of paper he is holding.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.599
"So, I was going to bed, and my brother told
me, 'Goodnight!

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:33.730
Don't let the bedbugs stick their proboscis
in your skin and suck your blood!”

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.640
D-504-3 pauses for a beat.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.530
"Good luck on a healthy dermis!” he ends
the joke.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.600
For two seconds there is no reaction from
SCP-504.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.870
Dr. Blast thinks this terrible joke just wasn’t
one that SCP-504 could understand.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.760
Suddenly there is a loud crack!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.510
D-504-3 falls to the floor; tomato covers
where his face once was.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.220
When Dr. Blast and the other researchers go
back and slow down the video, they witness

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.879
the SCP-504 tomato traveling so quickly that
it broke the sound barrier.

00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:06.730
The tomato impacted the joke teller at an
unfathomable speed, instantly killing him.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:10.610
Dr. Blast decides that he needs to be more
careful when choosing jokes for the safety

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.970
of everyone involved.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:17.100
Perhaps a crossbreed between SCP-504 and regular
tomatoes will yield different results.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.949
After the unfortunate death of D-504-3 the
research team waits a few days before experimenting

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:24.610
with the new strains of SCP-504.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.770
Three different crossbreeds are brought into
the room and placed equidistant from each

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.289
other on the table.

00:04:29.289 --> 00:04:31.129
D-504-4 enters the room.

00:04:31.129 --> 00:04:34.050
Dr. Blast presses the intercom button and
orders him to begin.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.389
"If you have dentures, don't use artificial
sweetener, cause you'll get a fake cavity,”

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:40.139
says D-504-4.

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:44.490
The moment the joke ends all three tomatoes
launch towards him at 145 miles per hour.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.389
They hit him square in the face.

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:50.949
Two teeth are dislodged; the test subject
is covered in the remains of the three squashed

00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:51.949
tomatoes.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:53.319
“Interesting,” notes Dr. Blast.

00:04:53.319 --> 00:04:58.009
“All of the tomatoes reacted in the same
way, so now we know multiple instances of

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:00.409
SCP-504 will go after the same joke maker.”

00:05:00.409 --> 00:05:01.849
He pauses to think for a moment.

00:05:01.849 --> 00:05:04.219
“What if we cut up the tomatoes?”

00:05:04.219 --> 00:05:05.830
The test room is reset.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:09.930
Another SCP-504 tomato is brought in and cut
up into quarters.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.490
D-504-5 enters the room and begins his joke.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.169
“I tried to walk into Target, but I missed.”

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:19.330
All four pieces of the tomato speed towards
D-504-5’s face.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:22.139
They slam into him at 212 miles per hour.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:26.330
One of the pieces of tomatoes impales itself
into his eye, instantly destroying it.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.800
The medical team rushes in and removes the
howling subject from the room.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.119
Dr. Blast writes vigorously on his clipboard.

00:05:32.119 --> 00:05:35.719
“We are starting to go through test subjects
too quickly,” he announces.

00:05:35.719 --> 00:05:39.499
“Let’s try a recording and see if SCP-504
will react to that.”

00:05:39.499 --> 00:05:44.509
The research team brings in a new tomato,
a CD player, and the "Harmful If Swallowed"

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:45.969
album by Dane Cook

00:05:45.969 --> 00:05:47.499
The CD begins to play.

00:05:47.499 --> 00:05:51.680
During one of the jokes the tomato launches
itself off the table and slams into the CD

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.539
player, causing both the stereo and the tomato
to shatter into several pieces.

00:05:55.539 --> 00:05:58.330
The tomato was clocked at 167 miles per hour.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.960
“It would appear that SCP-504 reacts to
recordings as well.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.960
We didn’t even have to deal with the damned
class-D’s in the first place,” says Dr.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:06.960
Blast.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.509
He informs his team that since the risk level
is now relatively low, they can continue the

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:11.869
experiments without him.

00:06:11.869 --> 00:06:14.180
He leaves the observation room to get some
rest.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.410
The other researchers look at one another,
mischievous smiles cross their faces as they

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.819
begin to laugh.

00:06:19.819 --> 00:06:24.930
The SCP-504 research team sets up three new
tomatoes and brings three Class-D subjects

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:25.930
into the room.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:29.529
The researchers then retreat back into the
observation area and begin a joke over the

00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:34.169
intercom system while the Class-D personnel
wait patiently in the room with the SCP-504

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:35.169
tomatoes.

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:39.289
“The following news item has just been released,”
said one of the researchers over the intercom

00:06:39.289 --> 00:06:40.289
system.

00:06:40.289 --> 00:06:41.969
“Bomb blows hole in Lenin statue.”

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:46.569
The first test subject finishes the joke with
the ending written on his sheet of paper:

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:50.099
“Ooh, that's gonna leave a Marx,” test
subject 1 says.

00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:53.559
The first tomato twitches, but does not leave
its location on the table.

00:06:53.559 --> 00:06:57.969
The second test subject reads from his paper:
“BBC is just Stalin the good news.”

00:06:57.969 --> 00:07:02.629
The second tomato leaves the table at 152
miles per hour and slams into the jaw of the

00:07:02.629 --> 00:07:06.159
second test subject causing a hairline fracture
and a chipped tooth.

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:10.369
The third test subject looks at the ending
to the joke on his paper and begins to shake

00:07:10.369 --> 00:07:11.439
nervously.

00:07:11.439 --> 00:07:15.099
He speaks two words, which he knows will not
end well for him.

00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:16.349
“That blows.”

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:21.559
The third SCP-504 tomato flies off the table,
slams into the third test subject's head,

00:07:21.559 --> 00:07:23.069
and instantly knocks him out.

00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:26.409
The test subject is sent to the hospital with
a massive skull fracture.

00:07:26.409 --> 00:07:30.800
The next day Dr. Blast bursts into the observation
room and reprimands the research team.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.190
“I thought we'd just established that recordings
work in place of live subjects!” screams

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:36.190
Dr. Blast.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:40.869
“I know how much you guys hate the Class-Ds,
especially D-504-012, but the poor guy might

00:07:40.869 --> 00:07:43.569
not even recover before his termination rolls
around.

00:07:43.569 --> 00:07:47.750
I'm making it clear right now that whoever
oversaw this round of testing is getting a

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:48.750
serious reprimand.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.289
The same goes for whoever leaked its video
logs to the staff!”

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:56.259
Everyone is silent, from somewhere within
the group of research there is a snicker,

00:07:56.259 --> 00:07:58.559
then they all break out into laughter.

00:07:58.559 --> 00:08:01.929
After this incident no Class-Ds, or other
personnel, are used in the research being

00:08:01.929 --> 00:08:04.169
conducted on SCP-504.

00:08:04.169 --> 00:08:09.729
The research team wheels in a television playing
the Sarah Palin and Hillary Clinton SNL skit

00:08:09.729 --> 00:08:12.800
The tomato shows signs of confusion as it
flies off the table.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.380
Its trajectory includes three separate bursts
of speed over 200 mile per hour, two stretches

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.879
of motion at normal throwing speed, and one
unprecedented instance of the tomato moving

00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:22.879
backwards.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:27.369
This all occurs during the flight of a single
SCP-504 tomato during the SNL skit.

00:08:27.369 --> 00:08:31.469
The working hypothesis is that the tomato
was unsure whether to take the video seriously

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:32.469
or not.

00:08:32.469 --> 00:08:37.630
The research team later finds out that SCP-504
really hates science and mathematics jokes

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:41.160
when they bring in a laptop that plays a pre-recorded
engineering joke.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:46.020
Over the speakers a mechanical voice can be
heard saying: “2009 is going to be a complex

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.020
year.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:51.040
We already know the real part; we still have
to find the imaginary part.”

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.660
At the conclusion of the joke there is a supersonic
blast and the computer is completely vaporized

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.450
by the tomato's kinetic energy.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:03.160
The sensors recorded an approximate speed
of 2,174 mile per hour as the tomato flew

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.290
across the room.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.480
The conclusion of the experiments on SCP-504
end with another computer being brought into

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.530
the test room.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:13.500
The computer begins to play the Monty Python
sketch of "The Funniest Joke in the World.”

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.560
Towards the end of the skit the Allied forces
are reciting the funniest joke in the world

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.710
in German to defeat the Nazi’s.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:24.370
The actors chant: “Wenn ist das Nunstruck
git und Slotermeyer?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.370
Ja!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.630
Beiherhund das Oder die Flipperwaldt gersput!”

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.140
At the end of the joke the tomato explodes
on the table where it once sat.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.550
Debris from the tomato coats the entire room
including the computer.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:40.200
The researchers conclude that SCP-504 did
not know what to do with “The Funniest Joke

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.660
in the World,” so it self-terminated.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:47.470
Dr. Blast sits in the cafeteria quietly eating
his lunch reading over the logs for the SCP-504

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:48.490
experiments.

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:50.780
Suddenly a commotion breaks out in the kitchen.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:52.110
There are screams of terror.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:55.790
Dr. Blast jumps out of his seat, runs to the
kitchen door, and pushes it open.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:59.810
To his surprise he sees slices of tomatoes
flying around the room.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.020
Someone on the research team thought it’d
be funny to give the unknowing kitchen staff

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:06.510
SCP-504 tomatoes to see what would happen.

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:09.850
After they had been cut up and put into the
food for the day, someone in the kitchen told

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:13.890
a bad joke; the tomato slices flew around
like shurikens.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.770
Dr. Blast sees a group of researchers peering
through a kitchen window and laughing hysterically.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:22.041
He will get to the bottom of which researchers
did this, and they will be fired from The

00:10:22.041 --> 00:10:23.570
SCP Foundation.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:28.220
Now watch “SCP-001 - Atonement - Ouroboros
Cycle (SCP Animation).”

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.170
Or check out “SCP-5000 Why?

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.650
- The Full Story Compilation (SCP Animation).”

